course: dictionary
lesson: 4471
title: Harmlessly: without hurt or damage
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Harmless means not able to hurt anyone or anything. Add -ly and you get harmlessly, which tells you how something happens: it happens without causing any hurt or damage. «A few swallowed whole pass through harmlessly.» The seeds go through the body and nothing bad happens.
explain: Use the words around it. Pass is something moving through, and the sentence says the seeds are swallowed whole and only a few of them, so harmlessly must mean they do no damage on the way. Check it: swap in "without hurting anyone" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Ask what the word describes. Harmlessly does not say what something is. It says how something happens. A ball can bounce harmlessly off a wall, so it hits the wall and nothing gets broken or hurt.
fact: Harmless means not dangerous, and not likely to hurt anyone.
fact: «Harmlessly» means without causing any hurt or damage.
fact: «Harmlessly» is an adverb: it tells you how something happens, as in «pass harmlessly», «bounce harmlessly» or «land harmlessly».
fact: Most small meteors burn up harmlessly in the air, so they do not reach the ground to cause damage.
fact: Most spiders in the UK are harmless to people.
exercise: «A few seeds swallowed whole pass through harmlessly.» What does harmlessly mean here? | With a loud bang | *Without causing any hurt or damage | Very fast and noisy | Only after a long wait
exercise: «A ball bounces harmlessly off the wall.» What happens to the wall? | It bounces back and hurts a window | It sticks to the ball | It is broken into pieces | *Nothing is hurt or damaged
exercise: «Most small meteors burn up harmlessly in the air.» Which word is the adverb that shows how the meteors burn up? | air | small | *harmlessly | meteors
test: Nadia says harmlessly means "very carefully". Is she right? | Yes, it means very carefully and slowly | *No, it means without causing any hurt or damage | Yes, it means very loudly | Yes, it means very quickly
test: «The joke was meant harmlessly, just to make everyone laugh.» What does harmlessly tell you about the joke? | It was meant to be cruel and hurtful | *It was meant to be fun, with no intent to hurt anyone | It was meant to be secret | It was meant to be heard by the whole school
exam: What does harmlessly mean in «Most spiders in the UK are harmless»? | Carefully | Quickly | Loudly | *Without causing hurt or damage
